1
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:14,770
[Connecting to You]

2
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:24,830
When I first met Chaonan...

3
00:01:24,860 --> 00:01:26,080
To be honest,

4
00:01:26,110 --> 00:01:28,110
I'm usually the one who scares people.

5
00:01:28,110 --> 00:01:30,289
It's rare for someone to scare me
like Yujing did.

6
00:01:30,289 --> 00:01:33,000
God, I really think he's insane.

7
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:35,680
How can anyone love so genuinely?

8
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:36,670
Among all my friends,

9
00:01:36,670 --> 00:01:38,450
there's no one else like her.

10
00:01:39,729 --> 00:01:41,380
She's kind of like

11
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:43,080
a female version of me.

12
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:45,900
It feels like fate is telling me that

13
00:01:46,090 --> 00:01:49,110
on this difficult journey of love,
I'm destined to meet

14
00:01:49,110 --> 00:01:52,420
-someone braver than me.
-It's good. A girl like her...

15
00:01:52,450 --> 00:01:53,650
Or maybe

16
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:57,130
-someone more miserable than you.
-is quite interesting.

17
00:01:57,530 --> 00:01:58,600
Let me ask you something.

18
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,350
I just saw some images.

19
00:02:13,210 --> 00:02:15,400
Oh my god, that's so creepy!

20
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:17,420
This is mind reading, right?

21
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:18,630
Am I right?

22
00:02:19,950 --> 00:02:21,710
Yes, you are.

23
00:02:22,570 --> 00:02:23,829
But you can't tell anyone!

24
00:02:23,829 --> 00:02:26,500
Why so nervous?
No one wants to know anyway.

25
00:02:29,130 --> 00:02:32,010
So, with a single touch of our threads,

26
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:34,640
you can actually find out
what we're thinking?

27
00:02:35,010 --> 00:02:38,010
I don't think it's really mind reading.

28
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:40,750
It's more like being able to see
the true thoughts

29
00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:43,750
two connected people have
about their relationship.

30
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,220
That's amazing.

31
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:47,620
Now that the Psychic Club's service
has upgraded,

32
00:02:47,620 --> 00:02:49,710
you should consider raising the price.

33
00:02:49,710 --> 00:02:51,000
Absolutely not.

34
00:02:51,030 --> 00:02:53,300
The 300-TWD price was set
with the gods' approval.

35
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,790
If we raise the price recklessly,

36
00:02:54,790 --> 00:02:55,850
we'll be punished.

37
00:02:55,990 --> 00:02:56,650
By the way,

38
00:02:56,670 --> 00:02:59,670
are Wu Dawei's secrets dark and scheming?

39
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:03,040
Don't come any closer,

40
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:05,480
you pervert.

41
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:13,440
After all this time,

42
00:03:14,610 --> 00:03:16,090
you still don't trust me?

43
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,480
You know his secrets.

44
00:03:47,510 --> 00:03:48,970
Right? Tell me.

45
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:53,950
It's his privacy. Can you stop asking?

46
00:03:53,950 --> 00:03:55,329
Well, when I mentioned him,

47
00:03:55,329 --> 00:03:56,579
you looked so nervous.

48
00:03:56,579 --> 00:03:57,530
I wasn't nervous.

49
00:03:57,530 --> 00:04:00,330
Come on, tell me,
is Wu Dawei's secret really dark?

50
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,410
If you ask again,

51
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:03,700
I'll tell others about your secrets.

52
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:05,540
No, when I said that...

53
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:06,640
Listen, do you know...

54
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:08,390
Fine, don't tell her!

55
00:04:08,820 --> 00:04:09,610
You win.

56
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:10,950
You win.

57
00:04:10,970 --> 00:04:12,380
I won't say anything.

58
00:04:15,690 --> 00:04:18,500
[The Seventh Thread]

59
00:04:18,529 --> 00:04:21,730
[Self-Deprecation]

60
00:04:19,990 --> 00:04:21,360
Dawei.

61
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:29,240
[If the Ending Is Uncertain,
Should We Even Start?]

62
00:04:25,210 --> 00:04:26,690
Has he left?

63
00:04:31,250 --> 00:04:32,590
That's a lot.

64
00:04:36,190 --> 00:04:42,270
[Dawei]
[I left breakfast on the table for you.]

65
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:46,740
[Police]

66
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,909
Not bad. I have to say,

67
00:04:45,909 --> 00:04:47,790
everyone in our team is good-looking.

68
00:04:47,790 --> 00:04:49,909
-What about the chief?
-The chief is

69
00:04:49,909 --> 00:04:52,080
a good-looking Doraemon.

70
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:53,000
I'm going to tell him.

71
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,290
Don't!

72
00:04:54,550 --> 00:04:57,080
Let's take this chance
to change the fan page cover.

73
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:58,210
Everyone is here.

74
00:04:58,230 --> 00:05:00,000
-Okay.
-There are other slogans.

75
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,420
-Xu, Pang, Senior.
-Pang.

76
00:05:03,450 --> 00:05:05,170
-Zheng, hurry up.
-Hurry up!

77
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:07,690
-One for each person. No changing.
-Come on, pick one.

78
00:05:07,690 --> 00:05:10,060
Come on, don't be shy.

79
00:05:10,090 --> 00:05:13,090
-Pick what you like.
-One for each person.

80
00:05:13,370 --> 00:05:14,220
Come on.

81
00:05:16,340 --> 00:05:18,090
But I'm not a police officer.

82
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:19,790
You rushed into the scene
to save our teammate.

83
00:05:19,790 --> 00:05:22,190
You're already one of us. Come on.

84
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:24,200
Lin Jiakai, don't waste time!

85
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:26,100
Lin Jiakai, hurry up!

86
00:05:26,130 --> 00:05:28,150
Come on. Hey, someone's
holding it upside down!

87
00:05:28,150 --> 00:05:29,520
Who?

88
00:05:29,550 --> 00:05:32,810
-Come on. Hey, it's upside down!
-There's something here.

89
00:05:34,970 --> 00:05:36,450
-Let's take the photos.
-Okay.

90
00:05:36,450 --> 00:05:39,950
-Come on. Three, two, one.
-Cheese!

91
00:05:41,409 --> 00:05:44,909
-Cheese!
-Three, two, one.

92
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:48,159
-Three, two, one!
-Cheese!

93
00:05:49,950 --> 00:05:51,540
-Okay, okay.
-How is it?

94
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:52,540
It's good. Look.

95
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:54,580
No, my eyes are closed!

96
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:56,540
You always look like that.

97
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:59,040
Jiakai!

98
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:00,740
Jiakai, your teeth!

99
00:06:01,980 --> 00:06:03,260
Did you just eat seaweed?

100
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:04,380
Is it obvious?

101
00:06:04,410 --> 00:06:06,610
Pretty obvious.

102
00:06:06,910 --> 00:06:08,970
-Dawei, help him pick it out.
-Here.

103
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:18,050
[Didn't want to work. Flew to Okinawa.]

104
00:06:18,290 --> 00:06:20,560
[Let yourself in
and help me water my plants.]

105
00:06:20,590 --> 00:06:23,910
She's such a rocker,
doing whatever she wants.

106
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:23,740
[Psychology Department Lab]

107
00:06:33,570 --> 00:06:37,150
[Psychology Department Lab]

108
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:48,940
Rainbow card...

109
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:05,090
Feelings and illusions are sometimes
separated by only a fine line—

110
00:07:05,090 --> 00:07:07,980
things may not be as you think.

111
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:12,230
Not as I think?

112
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:14,350
Then what is it?

113
00:07:35,909 --> 00:07:37,370
You're not going to sleep?

114
00:07:40,690 --> 00:07:43,180
It's okay. I'll just go back to my room.

115
00:07:45,659 --> 00:07:48,290
-Be careful!
-I'm fine.

116
00:07:51,870 --> 00:07:52,940
Good night.

117
00:08:11,450 --> 00:08:12,830
I'm off.

118
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:14,610
-Bye.
-Bye.

119
00:08:14,630 --> 00:08:15,960
Don't be late tomorrow.

120
00:08:16,420 --> 00:08:18,560
I've restocked the coffee beans.

121
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,630
Okay.

122
00:08:21,910 --> 00:08:23,570
Want some late-night snacks?

123
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:29,040
Lai said this fried chicken is really good.

124
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,540
Smell it.

125
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:33,840
It smells really good.

126
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:36,440
Yes, his recommendations never go wrong.

127
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:44,039
Why are you picking out the basil?

128
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:45,820
You don't like it, do you?

129
00:08:47,550 --> 00:08:49,510
I told the boss not to add it,

130
00:08:49,870 --> 00:08:51,330
but he still forgot.

131
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,590
You don't have to pick it out for me.

132
00:08:53,590 --> 00:08:55,000
I can do it myself.

133
00:08:56,860 --> 00:08:58,100
I'm almost done.

134
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:00,580
Thanks.

135
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:10,040
Are you...

136
00:09:10,060 --> 00:09:11,810
hiding something from me?

137
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:13,080
No.

138
00:09:13,150 --> 00:09:14,690
Why would you think that?

139
00:09:18,190 --> 00:09:19,290
Then tell me,

140
00:09:20,370 --> 00:09:21,810
did something happen to

141
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:26,640
the thread between us?

142
00:09:29,270 --> 00:09:31,070
You really don't want to tell me?

143
00:09:31,210 --> 00:09:31,920
Why?

144
00:09:31,940 --> 00:09:34,400
It's not that I don't want to tell you.

145
00:09:36,090 --> 00:09:37,150
It's just...

146
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:46,470
Sorry, I didn't mean to!

147
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,950
Is he the police officer

148
00:09:53,950 --> 00:09:56,080
who often buys coffee from you?

149
00:09:57,370 --> 00:09:58,600
He's also the one
chatting with that girl in a wedding dress

150
00:09:58,600 --> 00:10:00,140
over there last time, right?

151
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:02,390
Manager, you're so gossipy.

152
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:05,630
What? I'm just asking.

153
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:07,750
You two seem really close.

154
00:10:08,870 --> 00:10:10,040
No, we're not.

155
00:10:10,830 --> 00:10:13,160
We're just very ordinary friends.

156
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:13,960
Ordinary friends?

157
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:15,770
Would ordinary friends
have late-night snacks together?

158
00:10:15,770 --> 00:10:16,770
Manager,

159
00:10:16,790 --> 00:10:19,290
actually, we're not that close.

160
00:10:22,430 --> 00:10:23,260
Fine.

161
00:10:24,770 --> 00:10:26,970
-I'm done. We can go.
-I misunderstood.

162
00:10:28,090 --> 00:10:29,460
Did you wash it clean?

163
00:10:31,110 --> 00:10:33,380
Manager, thanks for letting me
use the restroom.

164
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:36,840
It's nothing. Jiakai's friends
are always welcomed to use it.

165
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:43,380
Never mind. Just give me back my shirt.

166
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:46,840
-But there's still a little stain.
-It's okay. Thanks.

167
00:10:51,270 --> 00:10:53,020
What's wrong?

168
00:10:53,050 --> 00:10:54,620
Did I say something wrong?

169
00:11:06,130 --> 00:11:07,170
Dawei?

170
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:19,570
Why isn't he here?

171
00:11:23,430 --> 00:11:24,930
Has he already left?

172
00:11:28,250 --> 00:11:29,270
Good morning.

173
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:34,710
Hey,

174
00:11:35,220 --> 00:11:36,400
why are you late?

175
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:40,810
The bus came a bit late.

176
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:43,140
Since you're late, you'll print this.

177
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:44,050
Okay.

178
00:11:53,950 --> 00:11:54,820
Dawei,

179
00:11:54,910 --> 00:11:57,370
didn't we agree
to have breakfast together?

180
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:00,070
I forgot.

181
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:05,840
We had a deal yesterday.
How could you forget?

182
00:12:15,870 --> 00:12:17,200
Have you had breakfast?

183
00:12:17,230 --> 00:12:18,770
I bought an extra one.

184
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,050
Do you want

185
00:12:20,070 --> 00:12:23,290
the pumpkin and mashed potato egg sandwich
or the pork egg sandwich?

186
00:12:23,290 --> 00:12:24,250
Eat it yourself.

187
00:12:24,430 --> 00:12:25,450
I'm full.

188
00:12:31,210 --> 00:12:32,670
[Expose the Collusion
Between Corrupt Officials and Merchants]

189
00:12:31,230 --> 00:12:32,850
Protect the old house!

190
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:34,110
[Fight Against Capitalist Monopoly]

191
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:34,340
Protect the old house!

192
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:35,610
Protect the bookstore!

193
00:12:35,610 --> 00:12:36,930
Protect the bookstore!

194
00:12:36,930 --> 00:12:38,280
Stop the urban renewal!

195
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:39,810
Stop the urban renewal!

196
00:12:39,830 --> 00:12:42,370
Fight against capitalist monopoly!

197
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:45,180
Fight against capitalist monopoly!

198
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:47,680
-Someone reported a public disturbance.
-Protect the old house!

199
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:50,260
-She's the leader, right?
-Protect the bookstore!

200
00:12:50,260 --> 00:12:51,590
Stop the urban renewal!

201
00:12:51,620 --> 00:12:52,940
-Yes, that's her.
-Stop the urban renewal!

202
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:54,830
-She's been protesting here for days.
-Expose the collusion...

203
00:12:54,830 --> 00:12:57,040
-That's why we decided to call the police.
-Between officials and Longxing Group!

204
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:59,160
-Why didn't you talk or disperse them?
-Unscrupulous Longxing Group!

205
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:01,890
-If we disperse the crowd,
-Unscrupulous Longxing Group!

206
00:13:01,890 --> 00:13:03,450
it will affect our company's image.

207
00:13:03,450 --> 00:13:05,510
So, it's better for you to handle it.

208
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:07,620
I'll keep reminding you of the importance

209
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:10,020
of preserving our architectural heritage!

210
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:11,520
We won't give up!

211
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:13,390
We won't give up!

212
00:13:13,420 --> 00:13:16,610
-We won't give up!
-Please stop!

213
00:13:17,290 --> 00:13:19,420
Miss, you're the one in charge, right?

214
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:20,830
What you're doing

215
00:13:20,830 --> 00:13:22,080
is already affecting others.

216
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:22,830
So what?

217
00:13:22,830 --> 00:13:24,790
Do you think we'll be scared
just because you called the police?

218
00:13:24,790 --> 00:13:25,810
We're just expressing our demands

219
00:13:25,810 --> 00:13:27,160
rationally.

220
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:28,380
That's right.

221
00:13:28,410 --> 00:13:30,000
You're just standing here

222
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,290
and repeating the slogans.

223
00:13:32,730 --> 00:13:35,050
No one truly understands your demands.

224
00:13:35,410 --> 00:13:37,080
Then, officer,

225
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:39,200
could you bring the boss
of Longxing Group out

226
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:40,920
to have a proper talk with us?

227
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:42,190
We'll definitely tell him

228
00:13:42,190 --> 00:13:43,870
our demands clearly.

229
00:13:43,910 --> 00:13:47,040
Bring him out.
Longxing Group, come out and face us!

230
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:50,660
Tell him to come out and face us!
Come out, boss of Longxing Group!

231
00:13:54,610 --> 00:13:55,670
What are you doing?

232
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:00,280
Those big bosses

233
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:02,200
won't face you unless they have no choice.

234
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,860
You know that well, don't you?

235
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:08,320
Why don't you tell us your demands?

236
00:14:09,660 --> 00:14:11,160
Maybe we can help you.

237
00:14:15,550 --> 00:14:16,720
Okay.

238
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:18,600
Then I want to know

239
00:14:18,830 --> 00:14:20,580
how you're going to help us.

240
00:14:24,830 --> 00:14:26,290
Let's have a word in private.

241
00:14:26,290 --> 00:14:27,530
Go to the police station?

242
00:14:27,530 --> 00:14:28,930
What is he talking about?

243
00:14:28,940 --> 00:14:30,190
What does he mean?

244
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:32,300
Here.

245
00:14:32,540 --> 00:14:33,250
Thanks.

246
00:14:39,790 --> 00:14:41,720
My sister and I have been running
Old House Bookstore

247
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:42,680
for five years.

248
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:44,500
We lost money in the first few years

249
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:47,410
and only started
making a profit last year.

250
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:48,720
However, the city government

251
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:50,780
suddenly decided to
work with Longxing Group

252
00:14:50,780 --> 00:14:52,380
on an urban renewal project.

253
00:14:52,410 --> 00:14:53,600
They asked Longxing Group

254
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:55,410
to slowly acquire all our land,

255
00:14:55,410 --> 00:14:57,740
saying they'll transform it into

256
00:14:57,810 --> 00:14:59,460
an AI technology base.

257
00:14:59,790 --> 00:15:01,450
It's a big development project.

258
00:15:01,450 --> 00:15:04,160
The city government and the consortium
must've communicated with you many times.

259
00:15:04,160 --> 00:15:05,660
Communicate?

260
00:15:07,290 --> 00:15:09,290
They only came here
to hold a briefing reluctantly

261
00:15:09,290 --> 00:15:11,910
after we started protesting,

262
00:15:11,910 --> 00:15:14,160
and they’re the ones
setting the purchase price.

263
00:15:14,160 --> 00:15:16,410
When I saw her outside the group,

264
00:15:16,410 --> 00:15:18,930
I thought she genuinely
wanted to keep the old house.

265
00:15:18,930 --> 00:15:21,050
But after hearing her words,

266
00:15:21,490 --> 00:15:22,760
I'm not sure now.

267
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:25,010
What happened to

268
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:27,580
the people who protested before?

269
00:15:28,410 --> 00:15:30,910
Well, they made a big fuss,
crying and shouting

270
00:15:30,910 --> 00:15:34,660
that they wouldn't let the consortium
take away their ancestral homes.

271
00:15:34,660 --> 00:15:35,910
And in the end...

272
00:15:35,910 --> 00:15:36,950
What happened in the end?

273
00:15:36,950 --> 00:15:38,540
In the end, the consortium

274
00:15:38,570 --> 00:15:40,540
raised the price by 15 percent,

275
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:42,410
and they sold quickly.

276
00:15:42,410 --> 00:15:45,270
Some even treated
their representatives to meals.

277
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:48,550
So, you're saying

278
00:15:48,790 --> 00:15:50,560
that girl over there

279
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:53,610
is just like the previous protesters?

280
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:55,010
Maybe

281
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:57,300
she's doing this just to raise the price.

282
00:15:57,950 --> 00:15:59,220
Is that so?

283
00:15:59,450 --> 00:16:02,290
So, how many households in your area
still refuse to sell?

284
00:16:02,290 --> 00:16:04,410
At first, no one wanted to sell,

285
00:16:04,410 --> 00:16:07,330
but Longxing Group
kept pressuring us this year,

286
00:16:07,330 --> 00:16:10,200
so many people had no choice
but to compromise.

287
00:16:10,330 --> 00:16:12,330
Now, only our bookstore

288
00:16:12,350 --> 00:16:15,830
and the two houses of our old neighbors
next door haven't been sold.

289
00:16:15,830 --> 00:16:18,450
But even if our old house
is the only one left,

290
00:16:18,450 --> 00:16:19,910
I won't give up.

291
00:16:19,910 --> 00:16:21,450
I won't stop protecting our house.

292
00:16:21,450 --> 00:16:22,450
Jiakai.

293
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:24,790
You can see the...

294
00:16:24,790 --> 00:16:27,330
-Yes, you have superpowers.
-Yes, the threads.

295
00:16:27,330 --> 00:16:28,660
Go take a look, hurry up!

296
00:16:45,790 --> 00:16:48,210
Looks like the emotional connection
tied to this object

297
00:16:48,210 --> 00:16:49,670
is really strong.

298
00:16:52,830 --> 00:16:54,170
Lin Jiakai.

299
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:56,630
Don't take her side
just because she's cute.

300
00:16:56,630 --> 00:16:58,490
Never mind, just go do your own thing.

301
00:16:58,490 --> 00:17:00,360
You, stop that pervy look.

302
00:17:05,150 --> 00:17:06,880
I saw you at the station, right?

303
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:09,960
I'm a student worker
at the police station.

304
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:12,240
Oh, right.

305
00:17:12,270 --> 00:17:14,270
Is your scooter not starting?

306
00:17:14,339 --> 00:17:16,880
Yes, I was wondering what to do.

307
00:17:16,900 --> 00:17:18,950
I used to ride the same scooter.

308
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:21,069
I know a trick to start it.

309
00:17:21,210 --> 00:17:22,630
Can you hold this for me?

310
00:17:22,810 --> 00:17:23,859
Be careful. It's heavy.

311
00:17:23,859 --> 00:17:25,020
-Okay.
-Thanks.

312
00:17:28,480 --> 00:17:30,200
After turning the key,

313
00:17:30,410 --> 00:17:32,330
kick it once,

314
00:17:32,330 --> 00:17:34,290
then kick it again immediately!

315
00:17:34,830 --> 00:17:36,230
Look, it worked.

316
00:17:37,050 --> 00:17:38,510
You're amazing!

317
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:44,920
I just heard you
talking about the old house.

318
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:48,910
If you need anything,

319
00:17:48,910 --> 00:17:50,740
I'll be happy to help.

320
00:17:50,830 --> 00:17:52,330
I appreciate it.

321
00:17:52,450 --> 00:17:55,660
But as the owners,
we have to deal with it ourselves.

322
00:17:57,330 --> 00:18:00,160
Anyway, thanks for
helping me start my scooter.

323
00:18:00,230 --> 00:18:02,240
It's nothing.

324
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:05,570
Time to eat!

325
00:18:08,790 --> 00:18:10,120
Aren't you going in?

326
00:18:12,540 --> 00:18:13,950
You go in first.

327
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:26,380
Hello?

328
00:18:29,330 --> 00:18:30,590
Did something happen?

329
00:18:32,290 --> 00:18:34,380
Your dad found me yesterday.

330
00:18:34,830 --> 00:18:38,950
He made a scene downstairs, saying
he wouldn't leave unless I gave him money.

331
00:18:38,950 --> 00:18:40,340
He found you?

332
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:42,040
I'm sorry.

333
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:45,040
So, did you give him money?

334
00:18:45,590 --> 00:18:47,230
I had no choice,

335
00:18:47,350 --> 00:18:49,390
and I was afraid he'd look for you.

336
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:55,040
Why don't you go to Auntie's place
and stay for a while?

337
00:18:55,580 --> 00:18:56,980
I'll make time to see you.

338
00:19:10,650 --> 00:19:11,650
You're back.

339
00:19:11,790 --> 00:19:14,700
The series we wanted to watch
is now on the platform.

340
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:16,160
Want to watch it together?

341
00:19:17,540 --> 00:19:18,760
I'm a bit tired.

342
00:19:19,050 --> 00:19:20,250
I want to sleep early.

343
00:19:20,580 --> 00:19:23,040
Okay, we'll watch it next time.

344
00:19:23,650 --> 00:19:24,910
You can watch it first.

345
00:19:25,490 --> 00:19:26,700
It's fine.

346
00:19:27,390 --> 00:19:29,720
It's way more fun to watch it together.

347
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:36,440
[Keke]

348
00:19:39,530 --> 00:19:40,690
Keke?

349
00:19:42,930 --> 00:19:45,660
Is this the girl protecting
Old House Bookstore?

350
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:47,320
Yes.

351
00:19:49,410 --> 00:19:51,040
Why does she have your number?

352
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:53,080
We ran into each other
on the street last time.

353
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:54,790
Let me answer the call.

354
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:59,040
Don't tell me you want to help again.

355
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:00,510
I don't.

356
00:20:00,540 --> 00:20:01,950
Don't overthink it.

357
00:20:02,220 --> 00:20:03,510
As a police officer,

358
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:06,110
I've seen a lot of people like her
these years.

359
00:20:06,190 --> 00:20:08,520
Whether Keke will sell
the old house or not

360
00:20:08,660 --> 00:20:10,040
depends on the money.

361
00:20:10,110 --> 00:20:12,170
Don't get yourself involved in this.

362
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:15,010
I didn't say I'd help.

363
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:16,990
Stop lecturing me.

364
00:20:17,330 --> 00:20:18,780
Give me back my phone.

365
00:20:25,290 --> 00:20:26,080
Hello?

366
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:27,740
Great, you finally answered.

367
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:31,450
I found out that Professor Zeng Youhao,

368
00:20:31,450 --> 00:20:34,080
who studies community development
and urban planning,

369
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:36,280
is a teacher at your university, right?

370
00:20:36,470 --> 00:20:39,090
Can you introduce me
or take me to see him?

371
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:40,280
Lin Jiakai.

372
00:20:40,660 --> 00:20:41,770
Listen,

373
00:20:42,220 --> 00:20:43,600
don't ask for trouble.

374
00:20:44,250 --> 00:20:47,790
Hello? Are you willing to help?

375
00:21:08,420 --> 00:21:09,700
This is Two-Minute Love Live Stream.

376
00:21:08,710 --> 00:21:09,520
[Two-Minute Love Live Stream]

377
00:21:09,570 --> 00:21:13,130
[Peggy Talks Love Psychology]

378
00:21:09,700 --> 00:21:11,790
It's fleeting, so don't miss it.

379
00:21:11,790 --> 00:21:12,120
I'm Peggy,

380
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:13,540
and I'm very happy,

381
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:14,870
because I just came back from Okinawa.

382
00:21:14,870 --> 00:21:16,580
It was amazing.

383
00:21:16,580 --> 00:21:17,610
So today, I'm going to

384
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:19,250
talk about a psychological theory happily.

385
00:21:19,250 --> 00:21:19,680
It's called

386
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:21,500
self-deprecation.

387
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:22,790
What is self-deprecation?

388
00:21:22,790 --> 00:21:23,440
Self-deprecation

389
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:24,750
usually happens to

390
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:27,370
people with low self-esteem.

391
00:21:27,370 --> 00:21:29,000
So, what are the signs

392
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,750
of low self-esteem?

393
00:21:30,750 --> 00:21:31,660
The simplest one

394
00:21:31,660 --> 00:21:32,310
is that they

395
00:21:32,310 --> 00:21:33,370
lack confidence

396
00:21:33,370 --> 00:21:35,160
and feel they don't deserve to be loved.

397
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:36,160
For example,

398
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:38,120
in a relationship,

399
00:21:38,120 --> 00:21:39,410
even if the other person
loves them very much,

400
00:21:39,410 --> 00:21:41,200
they will think,

401
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:42,910
"Am I really good enough

402
00:21:42,910 --> 00:21:44,910
to make him love me that much"?

403
00:21:44,910 --> 00:21:46,080
Or

404
00:21:46,080 --> 00:21:48,040
when they're dating someone,

405
00:21:48,040 --> 00:21:49,370
the closer they get,

406
00:21:49,370 --> 00:21:50,830
the more they might think,

407
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:53,410
"Will he leave me one day"?

408
00:21:53,410 --> 00:21:55,450
And they just want to run away.

409
00:21:55,060 --> 00:21:55,580
[Shock]

410
00:21:55,450 --> 00:21:56,410
Ms. Peggy, are you busy?

411
00:21:56,410 --> 00:21:57,540
Everyone,

412
00:21:57,540 --> 00:22:00,040
let me formally introduce
my little assistant.

413
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:01,450
Come on.

414
00:22:01,450 --> 00:22:03,410
Sit down.

415
00:22:03,410 --> 00:22:04,580
This is the perfect time.

416
00:22:04,580 --> 00:22:06,190
I'll let you ask

417
00:22:06,210 --> 00:22:07,120
the question today.

418
00:22:07,120 --> 00:22:08,430
If something

419
00:22:08,450 --> 00:22:10,160
is bound to fail,

420
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:12,080
should I still do it?

421
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:13,540
Is it about love?

422
00:22:15,700 --> 00:22:16,410
Yes.

423
00:22:16,410 --> 00:22:18,830
That's a great question,

424
00:22:18,830 --> 00:22:21,580
and I believe many of you
want to know it, too.

425
00:22:21,580 --> 00:22:22,700
Okay, let me ask you a question.

426
00:22:22,700 --> 00:22:25,030
If there's a delicious dish,

427
00:22:25,060 --> 00:22:26,080
once you eat it,

428
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:28,000
it'll eventually become waste,

429
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,330
or

430
00:22:29,330 --> 00:22:31,370
if you have a full meal today,

431
00:22:31,370 --> 00:22:33,330
you'll eventually get hungry again,

432
00:22:33,330 --> 00:22:34,830
will you eat it?

433
00:22:34,830 --> 00:22:35,660
I will.

434
00:22:35,690 --> 00:22:36,700
Why?

435
00:22:36,700 --> 00:22:37,230
Because

436
00:22:37,260 --> 00:22:38,870
I still need the nutrients.

437
00:22:38,870 --> 00:22:40,390
Yes! Everyone,

438
00:22:40,410 --> 00:22:41,620
did you hear that?

439
00:22:41,620 --> 00:22:43,370
Our little assistant is amazing.

440
00:22:43,370 --> 00:22:44,250
In life,

441
00:22:44,270 --> 00:22:46,040
whether it's love, work, or study,

442
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:48,290
what matters most is not the result,

443
00:22:48,290 --> 00:22:50,570
but the nutrients gained in the process,

444
00:22:50,590 --> 00:22:51,290
okay?

445
00:22:51,360 --> 00:22:53,870
Come on,
let's give him a round of applause.

446
00:22:53,870 --> 00:22:54,570
You can also get

447
00:22:54,570 --> 00:22:55,410
a small reward.

448
00:22:55,410 --> 00:22:57,500
Do you want to know what it is?

449
00:22:58,040 --> 00:22:58,450
Yes.

450
00:22:58,480 --> 00:22:59,910
I brought it back from Okinawa,

451
00:22:59,910 --> 00:23:01,130
and it's destined to become waste—

452
00:23:01,130 --> 00:23:02,120
it's ramen!

453
00:23:02,910 --> 00:23:04,250
Bye!

454
00:23:06,540 --> 00:23:08,000
You did a great job.
